==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpeɪtɹən ˈseɪnt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-patron saint.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{examples|sense=protector or supporter|
* [[Saint Patrick|St. Patrick]] (Ireland)
* {{w|Anthony of Padua|St. Anthony}} (travelers and lost things)}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|Christianity}} A [[saint]] [[conceive]]d as the [[patron]] ([[protector]] or [[supporter]]) of a [[particular]] [[place]], [[group]], [[person]], or [[activity]], for whom or for which his or her [[intercession]] is specially [[invoke]]d.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=8 July 2016|author=w:Wesley J. Smith|title=St. John the Wonderworker|journal=w:First Things|url=https://www.firstthings.com/web-exclusives/2016/07/st-john-the-wonderworker|text=My '''patron saint''', St. John of Shanghai and San Francisco—also known as “St. John the Wonderworker”—is particularly noteworthy in this regard {{...}}|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250120011616/https://www.firstthings.com/web-exclusives/2016/07/st-john-the-wonderworker|archivedate=20 January 2025}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} An [[exemplar]]: an [[individual]] who [[exemplifies]] [[some]] [[trait]] or [[group]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:exemplar}}
#: {{ux|en|Janet is the '''patron saint''' of procrastination. I'm thinking of erecting her a shrine of doughnut boxes in the breakroom.}}

